    <string name="onb_ok_title">You\'re all set</string>
    <string name="onb_ok_body">Every protocol is available to you. Fasts of 24 hours or more always come with a short safety checklist.</string>
    <string name="onb_soft_title">Please check with your doctor</string>
    <string name="onb_soft_body">Some medicines need adjusting when you fast. Please talk to your doctor before you start. Fasts over 24 hours will stay locked.</string>
    <string name="onb_soft_ack">I\'ve discussed fasting with my doctor</string>
    <string name="reason_glucose">Insulin or sulfonylureas can cause low blood sugar while fasting.</string>
    <string name="reason_sglt2">SGLT2 inhibitors carry a risk of ketoacidosis while fasting.</string>
    <string name="reason_bp">Diuretics and blood-pressure medicines can affect fluids and salts.</string>
    <string name="reason_glp1">GLP-1 medicines already reduce appetite and intake.</string>
    <string name="reason_other">Your answers suggest extra care.</string>
    <string name="onb_block_title">Fasting protocols aren\'t offered for you right now</string>
    <string name="onb_block_body">Based on your answers, fasting could carry risks for you, so we won\'t offer fasting plans. You can still read the guides. If anything changes, you can update your answers in Settings. If you\'d like to talk to someone, support is available.</string>
    <string name="onb_protocol_title">Choose your usual fast</string>
    <string name="onb_protocol_body">You can change this any time. 16:8 is a common place to start.</string>
    <string name="onb_notif_title">Want a nudge when your fast ends?</string>
    <string name="onb_notif_body">We only send reminders you choose: when a fast ends, milestones, and safety check-ins on long fasts.</string>
